### 3. External Secret Keys Wire Format
- **Presentation:** [Wire format for externally stored secret keys](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-openpgp-wire-format-for-externally-stored-secret-keys-02)
- **Presenter:** Heiko Schäfer
- **Draft Reference:** `draft-ietf-openpgp-external-secrets`

Heiko Schäfer summarized recent updates and proposed changes for `draft-ietf-openpgp-external-secrets`, which defines stub transferable secret keys (TSKs) pointing to external hardware (e.g., smart cards, TPMs):

- **Recent Changes:** When no locator hint is present, the key material is explicitly defaulted to "unavailable".
- **Proposed Registry Cleanup:**
  - Decouple the S2K Usage registry from the Symmetric Key Algorithm registry, closing the open-ended mirroring after code points 1–13.
  - Clarify the behavior of the legacy CFB S2K usage entry (verified against four interoperable implementations).
- **Locator Hints:** Add an optional `device_name` field (up to 63 UTF-8 octets) for user-friendly UI prompts.
- **Code Point Allocation:** Select a final S2K usage code point (currently using 252).
- **Discussion:** Andrew Gallagher supported the proposed registry cleanup as a beneficial drive-by maintenance effort. Daniel Kahn Gillmor advised the authors to apply the proposed changes and report back to the mailing list.

