### 6. Stateless OpenPGP (SOP)
- **Presentation:** [Stateless OpenPGP (sop)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-openpgp-stateless-openpgp-sop-00)
- **Presenter:** Daniel Kahn Gillmor

Daniel Kahn Gillmor provided an update on the Stateless OpenPGP (SOP) CLI interface, which is actively used for automated OpenPGP interop testing across nine implementations (including a new Haskell implementation by Clint Adams):

- **Pending Specification Updates:**
  - `sop encrypt`: For each `--certs` argument provided, an implementation may skip individual certificates it cannot encrypt to, provided at least one certificate in that input can be encrypted to.
  - `--keys` flag added to `sop encrypt` to allow encrypting directly to secret keys (mitigating K-OpenPGP key-swapping attacks).
  - Profile support added to `sop update-key`.
- **Working Group Adoption:** Stephen Farrell asked whether the working group should adopt SOP. Andrew Gallagher and Daniel Huigens strongly supported adoption due to its foundational role in testing OpenPGP implementations. Chairs agreed to take the adoption question to the mailing list.

